            <ArticleTitle>Coronary-to-coronary bypass using a free internal mammary artery: an alternative.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>757-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Paucity of conduit of adequate length or quality poses a dilemma in the occasional patient. We report such a patient, in whom we used a modified anastomotic technique using the normal right coronary artery for the proximal anastomotic site of a free right internal mammary artery graft.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
